                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I honestly don't remember when and how I got the game, but I recently played it for the Trading Cards and thought I give it a shot. But I'm sorry, as much as I like puzzle games, this is unplayable. And here are some reasons:\n\nThe language: Even though you set the game on a specific language it weirdly displays some Russian all the time. And I can't help but think, that some of the words might actually be clues.\n\nDifficulty: Besides the fact, that the game doesn't explain everything, which most of these games   usually don't need, it is incredible hard. You can restart the level, but that is problematic because  sometimes you unknowingly soft lock yourself. Especially frustrating is the fact that the  levels  I  played are rather long, which  wouldn't be a problem if not for the fact, that one tiny mistake let's you experience everything all over again. Which is especially sad when said  mistakes were made unknowingly. This is far beyond  the principal of Inquiry-based learning.\n\nBug and Glitches: Sometimes you don't  have to do anything, because the other balls just start to much on their own, giving you no time to react or think. If this is supposed to be a feature I would gladly pay for it to be removed.\n\nLastly game fun: I like puzzle games but this isn't fun. Technically I shouldn't complain if I don't know if I even bought the game, but even for that price I would have refunded it If I had the chance.\n\nI don't recommend the game. The \"Features\" make it unplayable and if you are looking for fun and cheaper puzzle games I'm sure that there are better options, but this this one ain't the game.",
